{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/360247-wod-france-new-kiths","id":360247,"title":"WoD: France New Kiths","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-05T09:41:15-08:00","id":360247,"title":"WoD: France New Kiths","content":"I recently came into possession of Le Monde des Tenebres: France, the French language World of Darkness supplement all about France. It has a chapter each on the original five game lines. I got it mainly to finish off my Changeling: The Dreaming collection. When I was flipping through it, I came across a delightful surprise - there are two new kiths that never appeared in any of the English language Changeling books! I can't speak French, so I scanned and OCRed the two kith write ups then ran them through Google Translate.<br /> <br /> As you'd probably imagine, the results from Google Translate ranged from clear to awkward to unintelligible. Thankfully, there is enough that came out somewhere between clear and awkward that you can get a pretty good idea of what the two kiths are about. I went ahead and posted the results. Here are links to the posts if anyone is interested:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/notes/charlie-cantrell/wod-france-kiths-morganed/10152745076864635\" target=\"_blank\">The Morganed</a> - a take on Merfolk that predates Blood-Dimmed Tides by a couple of years. They're different enough that the two could easily coexist. The Morganed seem to fill a more Siren-like role.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/notes/charlie-cantrell/wod-france-kiths-korred/10152755280954635\" target=\"_blank\">The Korred</a> - a dwarf like kith that are the keepers of lore and faerie traditions. I love their frailty, Truth! It is the complete equal opposite to Pooka's Lies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T11:54:21-08:00","id":360392,"title":"","content":"This is wonderful! I've shared it with the following facebook groups: <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/groups/434553209907776/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/groups/434553209907776/</a> and <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/groups/118778428292536/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/groups/118778428292536/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3920-sarah-rps","name":"Sarah RPs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T16:52:02-08:00","id":360751,"title":"","content":"bah facebook..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T21:46:46-08:00","id":360941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/360247-wod-france-new-kiths?p=360751#post360751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">bah facebook..</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed...<br /> <br /> Now if there is a way you could share your findings in a manner that is a bit more accessible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T06:36:53-08:00","id":361253,"title":"","content":"They're public blog posts. I can see about mirroring them on Google+, but honestly, there are so few people there I forget that it exists sometimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T07:01:49-08:00","id":361266,"title":"","content":"Got them mirrored. Here are the Google+ links:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://plus.google.com/u/0/102704540762203292497/posts/jbR2i5T2MTc\" target=\"_blank\">Morganed</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://plus.google.com/u/0/102704540762203292497/posts/7sVJ2TnxGmj\" target=\"_blank\">Korred</a><br /> <br /> Hope these links work better for folks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T07:28:56-08:00","id":361278,"title":"","content":"Thank you for that PookaKnight.<br /> <br /> I really like the Morganed and do agree that they can easily be used along with the Merfolk of Blood Dimmed Tides there is no reason for there not to be several types of Sirens out there after all the oceans are vast.<br /> <br /> The thought of Korred &amp; Pooka buddy cops is hilarious, there is a partnership guaranteed to be filled with all sorts of mayhem.<br /> <br /> So again thank you for sharing this find.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T07:12:37-08:00","id":363466,"title":"","content":"If any French speakers want to take a crack at translating the two kiths into English more coherently than what I can get out of Google Translate, please do! If the community can come up with a good translation, I'll turn it into a nice PDF like other pieces of cut content that are in my sig.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T13:14:20-08:00","id":363748,"title":"","content":"I'll stop there as my brain is about to melt. After a while I can no longer differentiate between languages.<br /> I tried to keep the lexical field, but my style is probably awfull after a while I tend to put english words on the rythm of french sentences. The quality of the base material isn't always helping. At least I think I have removed any nonsense. Feel free to improve upon this.<br /> <br /> Morganed<br /> (Those who are born of the sea \u2013 sing. Morgan / pl. Morganed)<br /> <br /> The ocean has always fascinated mankind and fed its imagination. Even today it remains a mystery, bearer of death as much as wonder, numerous are the legends that attest to the existence of fairies and changelings related to the aquatic environment. We find among them the Morganed, who live in the Kingdom of Swells* on the coasts of Brittany, who count among those that are the most involved in the real world. Away from the influence of king Sha\u00efl of Kevil's court, they conduct their own business from their fabulous caves or their chimericals palaces. Since the disappearance of Ys, the Morganed haven't foresworn the oaths that bind them to their Sidhe lords, which nevertheless govern them with circumspection since they dread an uprising that would sweep them as a tidal wave. The sea is a most demanding mistress...<br /> Mysterious and unfahtomable as their element of predilection, the Morganed are of an unpredictable nature. Often melancholic, they are also prone to devastating angers, legendaries among other Kithains. As the tide that continually recedes and advances the Morganed can be very stubborn, their grudges are often deep-seated and bitter. In return they are faithful in friendship and hate above all traitors and perjurers...<br /> Fascinated by the beauty of their women, they are very respectful of their partners... but also particulary jealous. Whoever dares to seduce one of these sumptuous naiads exposes himself to their anger.<br /> Masters of the ocean, the Morganed are proud of their freedom, but are not keen on humans which they hold responsible for all the ills that plague the sea. Often, Unseelie members of this kith do not hesitate to drown unwary swimmers in order to take revenge for all the sacrileges that humanity has perpetrated over the centuries. Devoted to their environment, they are commiting themselves more and more to humans business insofar as it concerns the defense of the seaboard and marine environment both threatened by tourism and real estate speculation. When they gather among the waves, the Morganed reveal themselves as playfull and lascivious. Enjoying the sun, they spend long hours frolicking in pods** in the middle of the reefs, hidden in the creeks and small coves.<br /> The location of the Kingdom of Swells as ment that this part of the country played an unexpected polictical role for the Morganed***. Unlike many other aquatic changelings, they retained many contacts with kiths who libe on the shores, moreover it is not uncommon for them to assume human form and take advantage of the night to visit taverns. Fiercely independent, they are very suspicious of members of the royal court of Shail for obscure reasons.<br /> <br /> *I'm not sure if the name &quot;Royaume des Houles&quot; should be transtlated<br /> ** ok this one is on me, packs is probably better.<br /> *** I'm sorry this sentence just doesn't make any sense whatsoever in french, so I translated it unaltered. May be it makes more sense with the associated background of the &quot;Royaume des Houles&quot; since I think I remember this kyth was developed for said kingdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4065,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4065-foebk","user":"Foebk","date":". 01-08-2015, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4065-foebk","name":"Foebk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T14:01:12-08:00","id":363769,"title":"","content":"Love it! Thank you for that! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T21:10:42-08:00","id":366009,"title":"","content":"Okay, so I'm a huge fan of Changeling, and have been since it was released, and I'd never heard of those missing Kith. So thank you, thank you, thank you for this.<br /> <br /> I took the translations I found in a couple different places (big thanks especially to Foebk above), edited it for clarity where I felt it was needed (and to make them more universal than France-specific), and added just a pinch of detail to the Morganed to show where they overlap and coexist with the Merfolk. I found some nice symbols for the kith that were fan-made, and did the following PDFs. This was made just for my own game use, but because I got so much from the community, I felt I wanted to give back so others could use it if they like. The following files are free to use, and if you wish to share them around, I have no objections.<br /> <br /> Korred: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0ByTqztGXLD-bXy1BM29yYmRLVHc/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0ByT...ew?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Morganed: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0ByTqztGXLD-bUHVqU2l4YTR3NFk/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0ByT...ew?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4715-crispengray","user":"Crispengray","date":".  Edited to correct links. 01-11-2015, 01:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4715-crispengray","name":"Crispengray","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T08:40:35-07:00","id":625536,"title":"","content":"Perfect! I'm totally using these for my current game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T12:42:25-07:00","id":627786,"title":"","content":"I've got the book, but my French is worse than a Spanish Cow's. (note:<i> You speak French like a Spanish cow!</i> is a traditional French insult. Louis XIV's wife was the Spanish Cow in question.)<br /> <br /> Has anyone tried to make Lutins (a traditional French Fee) into a playable kith? They'd be high dexterity tricksters with some light powers. I.e. they are associated with strange lights and sudden flashes of light. I suppose they create UFO's these days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T07:48:46-07:00","id":631178,"title":"","content":"Nice. Okay, well describe the fae mien. Then give them an Affinity Realm (Nature for playing with light phenomena, etc?).<br /> <br /> Then give them the equivalent of two Merits at around the 2-3 points Mark. Wikipedia says they can become invisible and are very good at travelling (flying without wings, breathing underwater, crossing vast distances). So I'd give them the ability to fly or swim without impediment at their normal running speed, and the ability to make themselves invisible on a successful Glamour roll (these effects are chimerical only but they can still invoke the wyrd as usual). You could swap the latter for the ability to control ambient lighting to give a -2 or +2 difficulty modifier to those who witness the effects. These could, if you're creative, give the effect of a UFO if combined.<br /> <br /> For their Frailty, take the equivalent of a 3-point Flaw. Wikipedia says they're vulnerable to salt, so perhaps salt causes them aggravated damage (one health level per turn of direct contact)?<br /> <br /> Then pick a kind of roll they can never botch (in this case, Dexterity?). Hey presto!<br /> <br /> Their other traits and abilities can be attributed to uses of Primal, Pyretics and Metamorphosis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T14:46:56-07:00","id":631570,"title":"","content":"I love these Kiths! I have used the Korred in my games many times over the years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}